      "text": "Turkish drone strike wounds 4 civilians in Syria’s Hasakah\n\nTurkish drone strike on a brick factory in the town of Sfeya in Hasakah Governorate, northeastern Syria on Oct. 4, 2023 – North Press\n\nQAMISHLI, Syria (North Press) – Internal Security Forces of North and East Syria (Asayish) stated on Wednesday a Turkish drone strike targeted a brick factory in Hasakah Governorate, northeastern Syria, injuring four civilians.\n\nThe Asayish’s Media Center said in a statement that a Turkish drone targeted with three shells a brick factory in the town of Sfeya in the eastern countryside of Hasakah.\n\nThe attack resulted in the injury of four civilians with multiple wounds. They were taken to the hospital for treatment, the statement added.\n\nOn Sep.17, a Turkish drone hit a vehicle on the road near the village of Hatimiye in the countryside of Qamishli, killing two Asayish members and wounding eight civilians.\n\nBy Stella Youssef"
    }
  ],
